# count-35.log: the gate-count model for format 35, the baseline for 5.10
# and 5.11.
#
# The spike's gate-count crate (`spikes/s5-recair/count` on branch
# `spike/s5-recair` at a2784b49), ported as for `count-hardened.log` and re-run
# on vos-core at 5.10a, the segment AIR of formats 35 to 37: 25 chips, without
# the fifteen CPU columns and twelve next-row masks no constraint read. Ported
# in a scratch worktree, not committed:
# - the chips are the AIR's 25, in `chip_idx` order; the window kernel's shape
#   is mask 0x01f9ffff (23 chips, every one but POPCOUNT and BITCOUNT) and the
#   full shape 0x01ffffff;
# - the log sizes are the window kernel's classes 1 (2^15 steps, 8 pages) and
#   0 (2^12, 8) as derive gave them in 5.8.0's window run; POPCOUNT and
#   BITCOUNT at their table size, 8;
# - a leaf verifies a segment at format 35's parameters (blowup 4, 40
#   queries, PoW 24, interaction PoW 8, FRI fold step 1, last layer degree
#   1); the window kernel's class 1 is also counted at format 31's 44 queries
#   and PoW 20, over the new width. A fold verifies leaves and folds at
#   format 32's (44 queries, PoW 20);
# - the recursion AIR's components are vos-recair-air's (5.8).
# The gate counts do not depend on the log sizes; the leaf, fold and wrap
# models do. Counts [measured], rows [model], memory and time [projected], as
# `recursion-air.md` tags them.
# Run on the Intel Core Ultra 7 155H, release build.

